# ZVIEW04 cross-check of the cause: with the browser open, a DIFFERENT desktop
# menu pick -- the first row under "Help" = MENU_BAR_GUIDE 51 (zview.rsh;
# menu.c:654 Menu_show_help, the ST-Guide call, which has nothing to show on
# the QEMU card) -- goes through the same WinDom MN_SELECTED routing as Quit.
# Observable: whether WinDom's desktop MN_SELECTED callback (MenuHandle,
# menu.c:687) ran -- it un-highlights the title. HEAD: "Help" stays inverted;
# fixed kernel: normal. (Run tags *-zv-guide; the kernels were built as
# *-kinj-zv-about.img from this file under its first name.)
100 parkbr
3000 mark A00_IDLE
3100 move 76 8
3400 mark A01_MENU
3500 move 100 28
3700 down
3703 up
6000 mark A02_BROWSER
6100 move 240 8
6400 mark A03_HELPMENU
6500 move 260 28
6800 down
6803 up
8000 mark A04_AFTERABOUT
8100 parkbr
8400 mark END
